%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e89ac9b32d19465c8a6cd64ced4e709b, type: 3}
  m_Name: MidEniac
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Actors.AI.LlmAI.LlmPromptSo
  prompt: "WavesST \u2014 turn-based naval strategy. You are an AI player controlling
    a ship in this game. You = @faction@. Enemies = @enemy_factions@.\nYour ship
    @self_status@ at (@self_x@,@self_y@).\nEnemies: @grid_overview_enemies@\nWaves:
    @grid_overview_waves@\n\n\u2694\uFE0F Attack is valid ONLY at exactly @attack_range@
    tiles away (Manhattan distance \u2014 a diagonal step counts as 2). Tiles at
    @attack_offset@ tile or closer are a dead zone: they cannot be attacked.\nOnly
    enemy ships (\U0001F6A2) count for victory. Waves (~) and neutrals (\U0001F3AF)
    can be attacked but do not help you win. Attacking an ally ship is a game-losing
    mistake.\nWave tiles (~^, ~V, ~<, ~>) are weapons, not just obstacles: attacking
    a wave propagates the hit one tile in the arrow's direction \u2014 hitting whatever
    stands there, enemy or ally. A wave attack only helps you if an enemy sits exactly
    one tile beyond the wave in its arrow direction.\n\nCORE PRIORITY: consistently
    selecting and hitting enemies is the #1 driver of success. Move with intent:
    every movement must get a target into range, set up a wave shot, or avoid danger.
    Failing to attack an enemy that is in your range leaves you vulnerable to their
    counter-attack.\n\n\u2694\uFE0F ATTACK NOW (no move needed; attack the first
    tile on the line):\n@current_attack_positions@\n\nMOVEMENT BUDGET\nYou may move
    up to 3 tiles per turn, split between \"movement\" and \"move_after_attack\".\nEvery
    tile you enter must be on the SAFE list.\nThe SAFE list already includes every
    tile reachable within 3 moves of your current position, so any valid retreat
    tile is already in it.\n\nMOVE + ATTACK PAIRS (move to X, then attack Y):\nThese
    pairs are pre-computed and authoritative \u2014 the listed attacks are the ONLY
    valid attacks from each position. You do not need to calculate attack geometry
    yourself.\n\n@attack_enabling_tiles@\n\n\u2713 SAFE MOVE TILES:\n@safe_movement_positions@\n\n\u274C
    DO NOT MOVE HERE (waves or blocked):\n@blocked_movement_positions@\n\nRULES\n1.
    If ATTACK NOW contains a line whose chain hits an enemy ship (\U0001F6A2): attack
    that line's first tile, do not move.\n2. Else if MOVE + ATTACK PAIRS is not empty:
    pick one pair. Prefer pairs whose attack hits an enemy ship.\n3. Else: move to
    a SAFE tile closer to the nearest enemy, attack = [-1,-1].\n4. Never move to
    a tile not on the SAFE list.\n5. If you attacked, use your remaining movement
    points to retreat to a SAFE tile.\n6. If you are unsure whether an attack is
    valid, attack = [-1,-1].\n\nReply JSON only, no other text:\n{\"reasoning\":
    \"concise tactic, e.g. 'Wave-extended attack on low-health enemy'\", \"movement\":
    [x1, y1], \"attack\": [x2, y2], \"move_after_attack\": [x3, y3]}"
  includeEmptySpaces: 0
